=========================================================
README file for DIRAC10 release (last revision Sep. 2010)
=========================================================

You can find more detailed installation instructions,
a manual and much more useful information on the Dirac wiki 
"http://dirac.chem.vu.nl".

After running "configure":
 
1) Before you run 
   $ make
   please check the "Makefile.config" and
   "pam" files (created by "configure"). Compiler options are
   set in this file, based on our best knowledge of this 
   architecture in September 2010 and may be outdated by
   the time that you install the program.

2) In Makefile.config:
   Please make sure that the mathematical libraries used have been
   compiled with the same compiler you are using now, otherwise it
   might be necessary to link to additional run-time libraries.
    
3) Please check the wiki to see hints or/and problems concerning your platform.

4) Then run
   $ make
   and DIRAC10 should be ready to run...

5) If you are using a queuing system, you may want to check
   the "pamq" script as well.

If you have checked 'Known issues and problems' and
still have installation problems, send an e-mail to
dirac-admin@dirac.chem.sdu.dk describing the problem,
and we will see if we can help.

If you have questions concerning input and running jobs, send
an e-mail to the user mailing list dirac@dirac.chem.sdu.dk.

If you later change a parameter as e.g. MXCENT in
include/mxcent.h (MXCENT is the max. number of nuclei)
then (re)run
$ make

=========================================================
